nly to the inclusion of Navistar as of July 1, 2021, as well as exchange rate effects.", "relevance_score": 0.7, "relevance_reason": "This paragraph provides relevant unit sales and sales revenue figures for North America, which match the table's focus."}, {"para_id": "VW2022_P2166d3", "page": 3, "section_name": "KEY FIGURES BY MARKET", "section_level": 3, "text": "On markets in the South America region, we sold 487 thousand vehicles in 2022, a decrease of 3.2% compared with 2021. Sales revenue increased by 40.2% to \u20ac15.5 billion due to mix and exchange rate effects.", "relevance_score": 0.7, "relevance_reason": "It discusses sales figures and revenue for South America, providing relevant data that corresponds with the table."}, {"para_id": "VW2022_P7d1991", "page": 3, "section_name": "KEY FIGURES BY MARKET", "section_level": 3, "text": "In the Asia-Pacific region, the Volkswagen Group's unit sales \u2013 including the Chinese joint ventures \u2013 increased to 3.6 (3.5) million vehicles in 2022. Sales revenue improved to \u20ac51.4 (48.7) billion. Negative effects resulting from lower volumes \u2013 not including the Chinese Joint Ventures \u2013 were offset by positive exchange rate effects. This figure does not include the sales revenue of our equity-accounted Chinese joint ventures.", "relevance_score": 0.7, "relevance_reason": "This paragraph provides unit sales and sales revenue figures for the Asia-Pacific region, aligning with the table data."}, {"para_id": "VW2022_P2667e1", "page": 5, "section_name": "BUSINESS DEVELOPMENT", "section_level": 3, "text": "The Volkswagen Passenger Cars brand delivered 4.6 million vehicles globally in fiscal year 2022. This was 6.8% fewer than in the previous year. The decline was mainly due to continued limited vehicle availability as a result of parts supply shortages.", "relevance_score": 0.7, "relevance_reason": "Provides specific unit sales figures relevant to the table."}, {"para_id": "VW2022_Paabad1", "page": 5, "section_name": "BUSINESS DEVELOPMENT", "section_level": 3, "text": "The Volkswagen Passenger Cars brand sold 2.6 (2.7) million vehicles in the reporting year. ID. family models and the T-Roc were increasingly sought-after, and the new Taigo was also very popular. The difference between deliveries and unit sales is due mainly to the fact that the vehicle-producing joint ventures in China are not attributed to the companies in the Volkswagen Passenger Cars brand.", "relevance_score": 0.6, "relevance_reason": "Mentions vehicle sales and differences in deliveries, providing relevant data related to the table."}, {"para_id": "VW2022_P91704d", "page": 5, "section_name": "BUSINESS DEVELOPMENT", "section_level": 3, "text": "The Volkswagen Passenger Cars brand produced 4.8 (4.6) million vehicles worldwide in 2022. In May 2022, Volkswagen Slovakia celebrated 20 years of Volkswagen Touareg production.", "relevance_score": 0.5, "relevance_reason": "Discusses production figures, which are relevant but not directly aligned with the financial data in the table."}, {"para_id": "VW2022_P0d6d2b", "page": 5, "section_name": "SALES REVENUE AND EARNINGS", "section_level": 3, "text": "The Volkswagen Passenger Cars brand increased its sales revenue by 8.7% year-on-year to \u20ac73.8 billion in 2022. The operating result before special items improved to \u20ac2.6 (2.2) billion, which was attributable above all to improved price positioning, positive mix effects and reduced sales incentives. Increased commodity prices adversely affected earnings. Upfront expenditure for new products and technologies increased. The operating return on sales before special items amounted to 3.6 (3.2)%. The diesel issue gave rise to negative special items.", "relevance_score": 0.8, "relevance_reason": "This paragraph provides specific sales revenue and operating results, closely aligning with the data in the table."}]

