Question:
Discuss the significance of green bonds in Volkswagen's sustainability-oriented financial strategy.

Context paragraphs:
[{"para_id": "VW2020_Pcad387", "page": 32, "section_name": "REFINANCING", "section_level": 4, "text": "The Volkswagen Group used a variety of instruments and markets for its refinancing activities in 2020.", "relevance_score": 1.0, "relevance_reason": "Discusses the variety of instruments and markets used for refinancing activities, directly relevant to the table."}, {"para_id": "VW2020_P109305", "page": 32, "section_name": "REFINANCING", "section_level": 4, "text": "In September 2020, the Automotive Division of the Volkswagen Group successfully placed its first green bonds on the market, with a principal amount of \u20ac2.0 billion and terms of eight and twelve years. The green bonds are based on the Green Finance Framework presented in March 2020 for sustainability-oriented financial instruments. The resources will be allocated specifically to refinancing the Modular Electric Drive Toolkit (MEB) and the new completely battery-electric vehicles, the ID.3 and ID.4.", "relevance_score": 1.0, "relevance_reason": "Mentions the placement of green bonds, relevant to financing programs."}, {"para_id": "VW2020_Pbc69dc", "page": 32, "section_name": "REFINANCING", "section_level": 4, "text": "We strengthened net liquidity through the placement of unsecured subordinated hybrid notes with an aggregate principal amount of \u20ac3.0 billion. The notes are perpetual. One note with a principal amount of \u20ac1.5 billion can only be canceled by the issuer after five years, while the other with a principal amount of \u20ac1.5 billion cannot be canceled until nine years have elapsed. The transactions will be partly used to refinance the hybrid note with a principal amount of \u20ac1.25 billion that was issued in 2014 and canceled as of March 24, 2021.", "relevance_score": 1.0, "relevance_reason": "Discusses the placement of hybrid notes, which is relevant to the financing activities."}, {"para_id": "VW2020_P8bc074", "page": 32, "section_name": "REFINANCING", "section_level": 4, "text": "In the US capital market, bonds with an aggregate principal amount of USD 4.0 billion each were placed with investors in May and November 2020. Notes with a volume of CAD 1.0 billion were issued in the Canadian refinancing market. In addition, private placements were placed under the automotive issuance program for the first time since 2015.", "relevance_score": 1.0, "relevance_reason": "Mentions bond placements in the US capital market, relevant to the financing context."}, {"para_id": "VW2020_P9baf93", "page": 32, "section_name": "REFINANCING", "section_level": 4, "text": "Official euro benchmark bonds with an aggregate volume of \u20ac2.15 billion were issued for the Financial Services Divi sion. In addition to this, private placements were issued in various currencies and regions.", "relevance_score": 1.0, "relevance_reason": "Discusses euro benchmark bonds issued for the Financial Services Division, relevant to financing."}, {"para_id": "VW2020_P2e8b93", "page": 32, "section_name": "REFINANCING", "section_level": 4, "text": "Alongside the placement of senior, unsecured bonds, asset-backed securities (ABS) transactions were another element of our refinancing activities. ABS transactions in the amount of approximately \u20ac3.2 billion were publicly placed in Europe. In addition, ABS transactions were issued in the USA, China and Japan.", "relevance_score": 1.0, "relevance_reason": "Mentions asset-backed securities transactions, which are relevant to financing activities."}, {"para_id": "VW2020_Pe061de", "page": 32, "section_name": "REFINANCING", "section_level": 4, "text": "The Volkswagen Group was also actively involved in the commercial paper market with several issuing companies.", "relevance_score": 1.0, "relevance_reason": "Discusses involvement in the commercial paper market, directly relevant to financing programs."}, {"para_id": "VW2020_P1b7c7e", "page": 33, "section_name": "RATINGS", "section_level": 4, "text": "Volkswagen AG's syndicated credit line of \u20ac10.0 billion agreed in December 2019 was drawn down during 2020. Furthermore, the syndicated credit line was extended by one year by making use of the first extension option. There is an option to extend the term by a further year until 2026 at the latest, subject to the banks' approval. This credit facility was unused as of the end of 2020.", "relevance_score": 1.0, "relevance_reason": "Discusses the syndicated credit line, which is relevant to financing activities."}, {"para_id": "VW2020_Pa9d457", "page": 33, "section_name": "RATINGS", "section_level": 4, "text": "Of the syndicated credit lines with a total of \u20ac12.7 billion at other Group companies, \u20ac1.3 billion has been drawn down. In addition, Group companies had arranged bilateral, confirmed credit lines with national and international banks in various other countries for a total of \u20ac4.8 billion, of which \u20ac0.6 billion was drawn down.", "relevance_score": 1.0, "relevance_reason": "Mentions credit lines and their utilization, relevant to financing programs."}]

